<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="015" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>B-5 slim summary, privilege flag and paging cursor</title>
    <phase>A BFF rework</phase>
    <gate>after 013 and 014</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; modifies SignalReadService.cs and the capability (.cs)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Single-component projection and cursor with an explicit contract (FR-05, FR-11) and the canonical row type WorklistItemRow to project from</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>D</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns SignalReadService.cs, WorklistItemSummary.cs, IDecisionCapability.cs, DecisionCapability.cs and DecisionResultMapper.cs in its wave; 020 touches none</parallel-reason>
    <deps>013, 014</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, unit-test, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add the slim list projection WorklistItemSummary (WorklistItemRow without EvidenceRefs and Steps, keeping InvoiceReview, adding PrivilegeFlagged read from sprk_privilegeflagged) and a paged Decide-lane operation with an opaque cursor on the capability, leaving the Console's REST worklist response unchanged.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in C# record projections, JSON size budgets and cursor paging.</role>
  <goal>WorklistItemSummary exists and serialises to at most 600 bytes at seeded maximum field lengths; IDecisionCapability.ListDecidePageAsync(user, cursor, ct) returns at most 50 summaries in Console order plus a next cursor; the privilege flag is read in the list pipeline without changing read rules or the REST response.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-11, FR-05, FR-04 (supports). Gotchas (project CLAUDE.md §6): WorklistItemSummary does not exist; the row type is WorklistItemRow with #2580's InvoiceReview member; the list pipeline does not select sprk_privilegeflagged (only DecisionCommitService.cs:313 reads it). Spec assumption: a Work Item is privileged when the Signal or its subject carries sprk_privilegeflagged; verify the exact source column here.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReadService.cs (add sprk_privilegeflagged to the list $select; carry it on the internal VisibleRow only)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/WorklistItemSummary.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/IDecisionCapability.cs (add ListDecidePageAsync)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCapability.cs (implement paging)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionResultMapper.cs (map the new cursor reason code)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Signals/WorklistItemSummaryTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/regression/Signals/DecideLanePagingTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReadService.cs (WorklistItemRow ~L119-141, WorklistInvoiceReview L145, steps 9a and 12)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCommitService.cs:313 (how sprk_privilegeflagged is selected today)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">IDecisionCapability list operation</dependency>
      <dependency task="014" status="pending">Commit members added to IDecisionCapability.cs first (file ownership)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">The REST responses of GET /api/v1/signals/worklist, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision-plan, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/suppression and POST /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision stay byte-for-byte unchanged: task 011's contract baseline tests pass with no golden-file edit (FR-09).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">SignalReadService read rules are unchanged: the only list-pipeline change is selecting sprk_privilegeflagged and carrying it to the summary; the core-record check, Do-lane scope and 503 too_many_signals behaviour stay as they are; #2580's single batched BillingEventRead per response stays one.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">WorklistItemRow's JSON (the Console REST response) gains no member; PrivilegeFlagged exists only on the internal row and on WorklistItemSummary.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Page size is at most 50 summaries; order is exactly the order SignalReadService returns for the Console; the cursor is opaque (base64url of the last item's ordering key and id) and stateless.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">A malformed or tampered cursor returns a failure with the new reason code ontology.worklist.cursor_invalid, registered in DecisionResultMapper with an MCP mapping test; a stale but well-formed cursor is not an error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every operation this task adds or changes takes the caller from the request. Capability methods receive the HttpContext the REST endpoint already has (or its ClaimsPrincipal where that is enough) and pass it to the existing decision services unchanged. A null HttpContext or an unauthenticated caller returns DataverseUserClientErrorCodes.UserContextRequired (DATAVERSE_USER_CONTEXT_REQUIRED), and nothing falls back to an app-only client (FR-10 as amended 2026-11-07, option C; ADR-002 WP-6 fail closed). No ICallerContext or other caller holder is introduced.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every PR from this task that touches Services/Signals/**, Api/Signals/** or the worklist route is reviewed by spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 before merge (project CLAUDE.md §4); run /conflict-check before opening it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/FAILURE-MODES.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/pre-pipeline-context.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Dataverse $select is all-or-nothing" location=".claude/FAILURE-MODES.md">G-13: adding sprk_privilegeflagged to a $select fails the whole read if the column name is wrong; verify the column on sprk_signal (and the subject) first.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Optional field drift" location=".claude/FAILURE-MODES.md">AP-2: an optional field two clients read differently; keep invoiceReview's shape identical to WorklistItemRow's.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Verify the privilege source: confirm sprk_signal.sprk_privilegeflagged and whether the subject entity carries its own flag; record the finding in notes/decisions.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the column to the list pipeline's $select and to the internal VisibleRow; leave WorklistItemRow's serialised shape unchanged.</step>
    <step order="3">Create WorklistItemSummary (all WorklistItemRow members except EvidenceRefs and Steps, keeping InvoiceReview, plus PrivilegeFlagged).</step>
    <step order="4">Add ListDecidePageAsync(ClaimsPrincipal user, string? cursor, CancellationToken ct) to the capability (the caller comes from the request principal, as for ListDecideAsync; FR-10 option C): page of at most 50 summaries in Console order, next cursor or null; add ontology.worklist.cursor_invalid to the mapper.</step>
    <step order="5">Write the tests in the acceptance criteria (seed 200 items across at least 3 matters with maximum-length fields).</step>
    <step order="6">Run 011's baselines and the Signals suites; measure the publish-size delta; open the PR for ontology review.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="8">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the privilege flag on the subject lives in a different column or entity than sprk_privilegeflagged on sprk_signal, STOP and escalate with the evidence before choosing (spec Assumptions: 'verify the exact source column').</trigger>
    <trigger>If a summary row cannot fit 600 bytes at maximum field lengths without dropping a field the widget needs, STOP and escalate with the measured sizes.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>WorklistItemRow (SignalReadService.cs ~L119-141), 1–2 KB per row with EvidenceRefs and Steps; no type named WorklistItemSummary exists (grep -rn WorklistItemSummary src returns nothing).</existing>
    <extension>It is a projection of the existing row, not a new model; extending WorklistItemRow itself would change the Console's REST response (FR-09).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>30–50 full rows exceed Cowork's 64 KiB inline cap, so spaarke_show_decisions cannot return page 1, and FR-04 cannot be met because the list never reads the privilege flag.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/WorklistItemSummary.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCapability.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/domain/Signals/WorklistItemSummaryTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/regression/Signals/DecideLanePagingTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A WorklistItemSummary at the seeded maximum field lengths (including InvoiceReview with both ids) serialises to at most 600 bytes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With 200 seeded Decide-lane items, every page holds at most 50 summaries and serialises under 64 KiB.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Paging from a null cursor to the end returns every item exactly once, in the same order as SignalReadService's Console list for the same caller.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: when items are resolved between page requests, the stale cursor returns the remaining items with no duplicate and no error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a malformed or tampered cursor returns ontology.worklist.cursor_invalid; DecisionResultMapper maps it to an isError tool error (unit test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">PrivilegeFlagged is true on summaries of seeded privileged Signals and false otherwise.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">011's worklist baseline passes with no golden change; the one-batched-BillingEventRead test passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (at or under 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE) and the ontology review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec assumption 'page 1 carries at most 50 slim rows'. The new reason code name is chosen here (ontology.worklist.cursor_invalid) to follow the ontology.{area}.{reason} convention of DecisionCommitReasons; ontology review confirms it.
Completed 2026-11-07 in commit 4b23aec7fd. Decisions, deviations (the 600-byte row drops Sentence), publish-size delta (+31,767 B), tests (unit 4393, integration 153, ArchTests 1998 pass) and review outcome: notes/decisions.md, section 'Task 015'.
rework: fix-round-1 task 015</notes>

  <execution>
